From: dagu adaptation
Subject: freedreno: sysmem bypass when depth is unused

Chromium Ozone tags linux-dmabuf LINEAR. dagu-linear-mod.c forces GBM
pixels LINEAR so the contract matches. a6xx BLIT_EVENT_STORE still
writes macrotile into those buffers; ANGLE/Skia then sample them as
LINEAR (backdrop-filter snow).

Electron/Skia RTs are tile_mode 0, no depth test, 1-3 draws, no blend
bit — GMEM of those batches snows. Bypass GMEM whenever color is
attached and depth/stencil is not actually used. Three.js with a real
depth test keeps GMEM binning and does not CCU-hang.

CP_BLIT r2d during BIN_RESOLVE snows the whole window on a650; do not
use it as the LINEAR store.

Load via LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/dagu-mesa for Chrome and
Mineradio. Never replace gnome-shell Mesa.

Applies on mesa 26.0.8:
  src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -756,6 +756,24 @@ fd_gmem_render_tiles(struct fd_batch *batch)
    if (batch->tessellation) {
       assert(ctx->emit_sysmem_prep);
       sysmem = true;
    }
 
+   /* dagu a650: GMEM BLIT_EVENT_STORE into LINEAR color is sampled as
+    * LINEAR by ANGLE/Skia (backdrop-filter snow). Mineradio/Electron
+    * Skia RTs are tile_mode 0, zs unused, 1-3 draws, no blend bit —
+    * those batches must bypass GMEM. Three.js with a real depth test
+    * keeps GMEM.
+    */
+   if (!sysmem && ctx->emit_sysmem_prep && pfb->nr_cbufs > 0) {
+      bool depth_used = pfb->zsbuf.texture &&
+         (batch->gmem_reason & (FD_GMEM_DEPTH_ENABLED |
+                                FD_GMEM_STENCIL_ENABLED |
+                                FD_GMEM_CLEARS_DEPTH_STENCIL));
+      if (!depth_used) {
+         for (unsigned i = 0; i < pfb->nr_cbufs; i++) {
+            if (pfb->cbufs[i].texture) {
+               sysmem = true;
+               break;
+            }
+         }
+      }
+   }
+
    fd_reset_wfi(batch);
